Top-tier banks such as JPMorgan Chase, Bank of America and Wells Fargo together command a substantial share of retail banking IT outlays, reflecting their size, diversified product portfolios, and the urgency to replace legacy architectures. Their investment programmes concentrate on end to end digitisation, open banking APIs, and data centric risk management, generating a cascading demand across the supplier ecosystem. The concentration of spend among these three institutions sets a benchmark for technology roadmaps, prompting smaller banks to align their budgets with comparable standards and allowing the leaders to negotiate favourable terms with global vendors.
